## How to Verify a Vintage Marquise Ring Before You Buy

Three checks every ring must pass before you commit.

**Check 1 — Confirm the ring is modern-retail vintage-style (not antique shop)** if you want zero authentication risk. Major online retailer settings all qualify. Antique shop pieces require the full 4-step GIA Verification Protocol.

**Check 2 — Confirm V-tip centre prongs at order.** Vintage styling does not reduce tip chip risk. V-tip prongs on both marquise tips are mandatory. Most listings include this at $0 extra upgrade.

**Check 3 — Confirm the centre stone has a current GIA report.** For modern-retail vintage-style, this is default. For antique shop purchases, demand the stone be re-certified by GIA before purchase — $300 fee, 4–6 week turnaround, worth every dollar. [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) and [GIA 4Cs](https://4cs.gia.edu/) both verify loose stones.

I run these three checks before I quote any client on a vintage marquise ring. The modern-retail vintage-style route delivers the aesthetic safely. The antique shop route delivers the aesthetic with risk — buy only from authenticated dealers with provenance.

